From: F93k draft audit
Subject: [control] gate B dial publication before checking both UDP ports

Evidence-only correction for the G2 draft. It registers a completion callback on B before release begins. The callback verifies it runs on B’s owning event loop, signals entry, then holds that loop on an existing 10-second wait pattern. After the A callback gate opens, the test waits for B publication and checks both UDP ports while B’s loop is still held; the outer finally opens this gate before any channel cleanup. On the correct snapshot implementation, B publication follows its own selector pass and both ports bind. On the current-batch control, B can publish before that pass and its port remains bound. Existing assertions and loop-count-derived iterations are retained.

---
